    {
      "id": "e3199ccf-46d8-43a9-a67c-136f38c58988",
      "name": "Doc Panel 1 - Workflow Details",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1650,
        -40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "# \ud83d\udcd8 WORKFLOW DETAILS\n\n**AI Portfolio Review Summarizer & Compliance Risk Flagger**\nValue prop: turns an advisor's raw post-meeting notes into an objective summary plus a suitability/compliance policy check against the client's risk tolerance on file \u2014 not just a meeting summary.\n\nWho it's for: RIAs and wealth-management firms needing a documented, timestamped compliance trail on every client review meeting.\nProblem solved: suitability mismatches (concentration, risk-tolerance drift) go unnoticed until an audit or complaint.\n\nHow it works:\n1. Webhook - Advisor Meeting Notes Form receives the raw notes + risk profile.\n2. Normalize Input defaults every optional field.\n3. OpenAI Chat Model + Structured Output Parser feed AI Agent - Summarize & Flag Compliance Risk, which checks the notes against the client's stated risk tolerance.\n4. Shape Output is the single source of truth downstream.\n5. Log Review to Compliance Tracker writes the permanent audit row.\n6. Route by Compliance Risk sends high-risk cases to an instant Telegram + email alert to the compliance officer, and medium/low to a routine advisor summary email.\n\nExpected input (POST /portfolio-review-intake): {\"clientName\":\"J. Thompson\",\"advisorName\":\"M. Lee\",\"advisorEmail\":\"...\",\"meetingNotes\":\"Discussed moving 60% into a single tech stock...\",\"riskToleranceOnFile\":\"Conservative\"}\n\nExpected output: one row in the compliance audit sheet, plus a routed email (and Telegram alert for high risk)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bfbf42a9-965c-42e8-9e26-39a1f196b655",
      "name": "Doc Panel 2 - Setup Guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1650,
        800
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "# \u2699\ufe0f SETUP GUIDE\n\nRequired credentials \u2014 attach at these exact nodes:\n1. OpenAI -> OpenAI Chat Model node.\n2. Google Sheets -> Log Review to Compliance Tracker node.\n3. Gmail -> Alert Compliance Officer and Send Advisor Summary Email nodes.\n4. Telegram -> Alert Compliance Team (High Risk) node.\n\nSetup steps:\n1. Import and assign your firm's credentials on each flagged node.\n2. Replace the Google Sheet ID in Log Review to Compliance Tracker with your firm's audit-log spreadsheet (tab: Portfolio Reviews).\n3. Replace the Telegram chat ID in Alert Compliance Team (High Risk) with your compliance team's channel.\n4. Point your internal meeting-notes form / CRM webhook at the Webhook production URL.\n5. Review the compliance system message before customizing \u2014 this workflow explicitly does not give investment advice.\n\nHow to test: POST a mock high-risk note and a mock clean note; confirm both branches route correctly.\n\nEstimated setup time: 20-25 minutes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "aea7d61d-221c-43fa-abb1-605bd770616a",
      "name": "Doc Panel 3 - Customisation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1650,
        1500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "# \ud83c\udfa8 CUSTOMISATION\n\n1. Add a PDF-generation node to produce a signed, dated compliance memo automatically \u2014 edit after Log Review to Compliance Tracker.\n2. Connect to a CRM (Salesforce/Redtail/Wealthbox) via HTTP Request fed from Shape Output.\n3. Add a quarterly digest sub-workflow rolling up flaggedIssues into one CCO report.\n4. Add a second AI pass on Shape Output drafting the client-facing meeting recap.\n5. Swap notification channel: replace Alert Compliance Team (High Risk) (Telegram) with Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "09e0e1ec-6aa0-4582-93ae-244302f7bb10",
      "name": "Doc Panel 4 - Additional Information",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1650,
        2040
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "# \u2139\ufe0f ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nError handling: Sheets, Gmail and Telegram nodes use onError: continueRegularOutput so one failed integration never blocks the audit log or the other notification.\n\nAPI cost & rate limits: 1 OpenAI call per submission; all integrations run within free-tier quotas for typical review volumes.\n\nData privacy: only client name, advisor name, risk tolerance on file, and raw meeting notes are sent to the model. Stored data is limited to client/advisor names, complianceRisk, summary, flaggedIssues, recommendedFollowUp, and timestamp.\n\nKnown limitations & prerequisites: flags POTENTIAL mismatches for human compliance review \u2014 does not make compliance determinations or give investment advice; requires a Google Sheet already shared and a Telegram bot in your compliance channel.\n\nCreator: Swapnil AI Labs \u2014 swapnil.mandloi7@gmail.com \u2014 swapnilailabs.netlify.app"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
